Additional permission under GNU AGPL version 3 section 7
========================================================

Stud is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
or later; the full text is in LICENSE. This file adds a permission on top
of it. It only ever grants: if you never rely on it, Stud is plain AGPLv3
to you, unchanged.


The permission
--------------

  As an additional permission under section 7 of the GNU Affero General
  Public License version 3, the copyright holders of Stud give you
  permission to link or combine Stud with the Roblox Engine, and to
  convey the resulting work.

  "The Roblox Engine" means the software contained in the Roblox
  application package published by Roblox Corporation, and any library
  loaded from it -- software under terms incompatible with the GNU
  Affero General Public License, which Stud neither includes nor
  distributes, and which the person running Stud supplies themselves.

  You must still comply with the GNU Affero General Public License in
  all respects for all of the code used other than the Roblox Engine.

  If you modify Stud, you may extend this permission to your version,
  but you are not obliged to. If you do not wish to, delete this
  statement from your version.


Why it exists
-------------

Stud loads the Roblox Engine into one of its own processes, and Stud's
own code runs in that process. Whether that makes a combined work whose
distribution the AGPL would forbid is the old question about linking
against proprietary code, and it is a question nobody involved should
have to spend time on.

In Stud's case there is a good argument that it never arises. Stud does
not ship the engine, mirror it, or download it. The person running Stud
supplies the application package themselves, so whatever combination
happens, happens on their own machine and is never conveyed to anyone.
Every binary Stud does redistribute -- ANGLE, SwiftShader, the Vulkan
loader and validation layers, Android's libc, libm, libdl and linker --
is under a permissive licence, and each ships with its own notice.

This permission is here so that argument does not have to be made. A
distribution packaging Stud, and anyone building on it, can rely on the
grant instead of on a reading.
